label who are you
\doctor: ...Who are you?
stranger: I am a visitor of this place, same as you.
\doctor: Of this dream, you mean?
alien: Ah, so you’re sleeping right now?
alien: I have to make some conscious effort to come here, you see?
alien: Some people just slip up here unawares.
\doctor: Yes, I am sleeping. This is the first time that I have had a dream like this.
alien: It’s lucky then, that I found you here. Tell me, don’t you think it’s relaxing up here?
I remember how it felt a few moments ago, when I thought I was completely alone.
\doctor: Yes, you’re right. There’s just… too much stuff going on in my life right now.\
It’s not been easy.
jump perguntas
label WHERE ARE WE?
\doctor: Where are we supposed to be?
stranger: In a spot somewhere in the universe. I don’t know exactly. But it has so many different things to see.
audio music -
\doctor: But how did you end up here, if you say you’re not dreaming?
audio music "res://arts/sfx/chapters.wav" [loop="false"]
stranger: I found the path to this place one day, when I was at the worst moment of my life. I have come here ever since. To stay… and look.
jump perguntas
label WHY CAN”T I SEE YOU?
\doctor: Tell me… how come I can’t see you?
stranger: I don’t know. I never met anyone here before. Maybe you’re just not used to it. If you make an effort, maybe you’ll see me.
\doctor: Okay, I’ll try…
\doctor: …
\doctor: Okay, this is hopeless. I can’t see you. I thought you could control things in dreams.
I forgot that I’m naked right now.
stranger: Don’t be shy! You look pretty!
\doctor: Wait, does that mean… you can see me?
\doctor: “I- uh, would like you to look away, or something…”
Promise I’m not looking…
This is a very embarrassing dream
jump perguntas
label return
stranger: I don’t know how or why you came here, buI can show you my favorite views. Look over there, that pink spot on your left.
stranger: It happens to be a galaxy that has died a million years ago. One day, its light will no longer reach us. But you and I will be long gone.
\doctor: That’s sad. I didn’t even get the chance to learn about it before it was gone. Now, I know I never will.
stranger: Do you have to understand something to appreciate its beauty?
\doctor: Yes, actually. The beauty is in understanding the intricacies of a thing, its ins and outs.
\doctor: A mere surface level first impression can’t be actually called beautiful.
stranger: Is this place not beautiful?
- YES
