label YES
\doctor: ... I guess I was being too serious back there.
\doctor: I can’t deny that there is some beauty to this view. I’ve never seen a place like this. If anything, it makes me happy that I dreamt about it.
\doctor: I don’t want to forget it when I wake up.
stranger: I don’t want to forget it, either.
jump return 2
label NO
\doctor: I stand by what I said. Something so vague and abstract, I can’t make sense of it.
\doctor: If I could only know which part of the sky I was looking at, I could at least say something about it. In any case, I’ll probably forget about it when I wake up.
stranger: I hope you end up here again, then. So I can show you everything I know, and maybe you will learn to appreciate its beauty.
\doctor: You really want me to give in, don’t you? Okay, If I come here again, I will let you try.
label return 2
